<title>GERMANY: Germany details HCPI index Jan 1996-Jan 1997.</title>
<headline>Germany details HCPI index Jan 1996-Jan 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office released the following detailed comparison of its consumer price data compared to the harmonised consumer price index released by the European Union. All comparisons in percent against the year-earlier period.</p>
<p> MONTH	     HARMONISED CPI	GERMAN CPI</p>
<p>		    (Basis 1996=100)   (Basis 1991=100)</p>
<p> January  1997	1.7			 1.8</p>
<p> December 1996	1.2			 1.4</p>
<p> November	     1.3			 1.4</p>
<p> October		1.2			 1.5</p>
<p> September	    1.1			 1.4</p>
<p> August		 1.2			 1.4</p>
<p> July		   1.2			 1.6</p>
<p> June		   1.1			 1.4</p>
<p> May		    1.3			 1.7</p>
<p> April		  1.2			 1.5</p>
<p> March		  1.4			 1.7</p>
<p> February	     1.2			 1.6</p>
<p> January		1.2			 1.5</p>
<p>NOTE - European Union leaders will decide early in 1998 on the basis of harmonised economic data which countries qualify to join European economic and monetary union.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
